What's different now: No WebView at all. The flow is:

    Tap "Open MetaMask" → fetches nonce → opens MetaMask via deep link
    MetaMask signs → redirects back to chainpay://wallet-connect?address=...&signature=...
    App catches the callback, sends to backend for real cryptographic verification

On a real phone with MetaMask installed this works fully. If MetaMask's deep link callback doesn't return the signature (some MetaMask versions handle this differently), it automatically offers a manual address fallback so you're never stuck. The fallback sends 0x00 so your backend needs dev-mode bypass for that — do you want me to add that to walletController.js too?
