How it now works:

    Tap "Open MetaMask Signing Page" → app fetches nonce, opens http://192.168.255.34:4000/connect/ in your phone's real browser
    Browser page loads WalletConnect v2 → shows QR → MetaMask scans it and signs
    Page posts wallet + signature directly to your backend (POST /api/v1/wallet)
    On success, page redirects to chainpay://wallet-connect?address=0x...&success=1
    App catches that deep link, updates state, goes to dashboard

This works because the browser has no localStorage restrictions, WalletConnect loads properly over HTTP, and MetaMask can respond to it. The phone and your laptop must be on the same WiFi for the 192.168.255.34 IP to work.
